              "summary": "The 650, 550 and 430 nm bands approximate visible color. Bright terrain clips to white; shadows and color offsets remain."
            },
            {
              "id": "ratios",
              "label": "Spectral ratios",
              "description": "DLR’s published Clementine-style composite of photometrically corrected Dawn images: red is 749/438 nm, green is 749/917 nm, and blue is 438/749 nm. Colors emphasize spectral differences; they are not natural color or a mineral-abundance measurement. Original seams and color fringes remain. Exact black is treated as likely fill, so some dark observations may also be withheld; gaps use the gray grid.",
